  "_doc": "His medical books (#819; refs experiments/prop_lab/refs/doctor/): a shelf's row standing spine out (+z), 53 cm of them. The standard American texts a country doctor of 1882 owned: Gray'S Anatomy (Gray); System Of Surgery Vol. I (Gross); System Of Surgery Vol. Ii (Gross); Practice Of Medicine (Flint); Medical Dictionary (Dunglison); Human Physiology (Dalton); Diseases Of Women (Thomas); Diseases Of Children (Meigs & Pepper); Gunshot Wounds (Longmore). Most in law sheep (tan sheepskin with a red and a black label lettered in gilt, the trade binding of medical books into the 1880s), some in publishers' cloth, a few in calf. Each book a member (wood `paper`: ~1.5 kg an octavo): it burns, a ball goes through it, the row comes down with its shelf. Drawn from glb:medical_books, every face printed on its own sheet (tools/blender/props/doctor_d3.py: Pillow, as the bottles' labels). Written by tools/props/doctor.py.",
